            <ArticleTitle>Combined coronary and bilateral carotid stenting: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>202-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a patient who underwent stenting of both internal carotid arteries and two coronary arteries. Two combined carotid and coronary procedures were done 4 wk apart to revascularize the patient. The first procedure was complicated by a minor stroke with good recovery. At 6 mo of follow-up, he is asymptomatic and without angiographic restenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
